  "body": "Part of #4023. Step K5 of the record (K0, #4024; in `RECOMMENDED.md` under the heading `#4024`, migration order). It is delivered on `side/path-kernel` (AGENTS.md **Side branch**). It builds on K1 (#4025, the region model).\n\n## What to do\n\nAdd the entry and exit stage to `camcraft-pathkernel`, behind the trait `EntryPlanner`, with the `Exit` type.\n\n- An entry is one of: in air outside the stock, in a pre-drilled hole, in a column that is already cut, or a helix or a ramp into solid material that the user selected. Each entry carries its proof, and the moves stay in the proved place (law 5).\n- If no entry is safe, the operation is refused with a named reason. No entry into material occurs without a proof.\n- An entry of a different kind than the user asked for is a named fallback (law 4). The stage needs a way to name it: the law suite of #4027 reports that `EntryPlanner::entry` cannot name a fallback today.\n- The exit is part of this stage (maintainer answer on the record): a lead-out in the plane where there is room, then the retract.\n- The laws of #3746 (enter in air outside the stock box, then an arc lead-in in the cut plane), #3759 (air entries of Face and the 2D Adaptive Outside plan) and #3397 are covered by this stage.\n- For the material side Outside, the tool centre can go to the stock outline (maintainer, 2026-11-26: \"Yes, to the edge\"). A clamp at the edge is a keep-out.\n- No old planner changes. With the default switch the output is identical.\n\n## Pins\n\n- The stage is registered in the law suite (#4027) and passes L4 and L5.\n- A closed pocket with no hole and no user helix or ramp is refused by name. An open pocket enters in air.\n- Negative tests: a proof for a different place is refused; a plunge into solid material without the user's choice is refused.\n\n## Done means\n\nThe entry and exit stage is on the side branch with its pins green. The first recipe (2D Pocket, #3752) can then start when K2 and K4 are also on the branch.\n",
